Pickup rules
------------

The plugin reads the ownership flag the server already sends with every ground
item, exposed as net.runelite.api.TileItem, and the ironman varbit exposed as
net.runelite.api.gameval.VarbitID. Nothing about ironman restrictions is
reimplemented or predicted here.

RuneLite's own Ground Items plugin applies the same test to its overlay text
under its OwnershipFilterMode.TAKEABLE setting:

  Ground Items, Copyright (c) 2017, Aria <aria@ariamoded.net>
  and the RuneLite contributors, BSD 2-Clause

That was read as confirmation the flag means what it appears to mean, and the
group ownership case was settled from it. No code from it is reproduced; this
plugin hides models and menu entries, which it does not.

Restrictions were checked against the OSRS Wiki on 2026-09-17:

  https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ironman_Mode

No wiki text or images are redistributed here. A published rule can go stale,
which is the reason the ownership flag is read rather than summarised.

Scope
-----

This plugin has not been reviewed by Jagex or by the RuneLite Plugin Hub. The
existence of comparable Hub plugins that hide ground item models is evidence
that the functionality exists, not approval of this implementation. It removes
options the server would have refused; it performs no action on their behalf.
